  "details": "Using Windows Mixed Reality Headset (HP 1440 developer edition)\n\nSimply enter any world. Usually, it is fine for a few minutes, then gets worse over time. These flickers seem to sometimes be accompanied by small spikes on the GPU performance graph in the fpsVR overlay, though I am unsure if that was related.\n\n---\n\n(update2:) After further investigation, this is actually two separate issues. The information below update1 and the new clip demonstrate SyncPulse's Pimax issue, which has now been resolved for both Pimax and WMR.\n\nThis post is for the issue listed above, where it seems like the game flickers between the current and previous orientation as you rotate, but only at seemingly random times for similarly random durations.\n\nIt feels like if reprojection was kind of broken, but it happens even while the framerate is locked at 90. This flicker only happens in VRChat's view, the SteamVR dashboard and WMR start menu do not flicker on rotation.\n\nThis still occurs up to the current beta [Build 1381], though at this point I may have built up a tolerance to it so I don't notice as much.\n\n---\n\n(update1:) It seems they occur at specific angles, see the (New clip) video at the bottom for a better clip.\n\nEvery now and then the viewpoint flicks to an incorrect orientation for a few frames and back again. The issue does not occur on Live's Unity 2019.\n\nUnsure if it can be fixed on VRChat's end, as it also occurs in Zenith MMO (Unity 2021), meaning it may be an issue across newer Unity releases such as the one this Open Beta is testing (Unity 2022).\n\nVideo demonstration:\n\n(New clip) https://youtu.be/Wq8NuguTfMo\n\n(Old clip) https://youtu.be/ixCQ4awbGqI",
